<title>USA: TRW sets two-for-one split, boosts dividend.</title>
<headline>TRW sets two-for-one split, boosts dividend.</headline>
<dateline>CLEVELAND</dateline>
<text>
<p>TRW Inc., the automotive and defence parts maker, said Wednesday its board had approved a two-for-one stock split, and boosted its quarterly dividend.</p>
<p>The split will increase the number of outstanding common shares to 126.4 million, TRW said.</p>
<p>The company said its dividend was increased to 31 cents a share on post-split shares, or 62 cents per share on a pre-split basis. The company previously paid 55 cents a share. The dividend is payable on Dec. 9.</p>
<p>TRW's stock was up 62.5 cents to $91 on the New York Stock Exchange.</p>
